 "change": "OriginalStateRecord's flat storage is one ManagedBuffer per record (Flat: the bytes, then one definedness bit per byte, then 8 zero pad bytes; header {count, whole-array cache}); the record stays 40 bytes (flat: Flat?, flatCount, large: Large?). Reads check range, mask and value with one load each in the same order as before; writes and overwrites copy a shared buffer once (or clear the cache of a unique one) and return early when the bytes and definedness are already there; copies copy the bytes and mask once without zero-filling first; the mask is packed byte-wise; `bytes`/`defined` whole reads are built once per written version (FlatWhole, under flatWholeLock) so loops indexing them stay linear; storageIdentity returns the buffer address twice; sharesStorage compares buffers",
 "profile_after": "rts2b-vs-dwarf (6,195 main-thread samples): _consumeAndCreateNew 4.96%",
